meta {
  name: Write a paper
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assessments
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Photosynthesis — end of chapter",
    "source": {
      "book_ids": ["{{bookId}}"]
    },
    "type": "mixed",
    "formats": ["mcq", "true_false", "match", "short_answer"],
    "levels": ["recall", "understand", "evaluate"],
    "rigor": "medium",
    "instructions": "Concentrate on the light-independent reactions.",
    "question_count": 4
  }
}


script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("assessmentId", res.body.id);
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
  res.body.status: eq generating
}

docs {
  202: generation runs on the `llm` queue, never in the request. Poll `Read the draft`
  for status.

  `book_ids` arrives in a request body, so every id is checked against `scope='canon'`
  *and* against what the caller may actually read. A book that fails either test refuses
  the whole request rather than being quietly skipped — an author who asked for four
  books and got a paper from two has been given something they did not ask for and no
  way to notice.

  Rate limited to `ASSESSMENT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR` (10/hour), checked before anything is
  written: generation is the most expensive thing in the product and refusing it cheaply
  is the point of checking first.

  **`formats` and `levels` are both optional, and omitting them is a choice rather than
  a missing answer.** Empty means *auto*: the server picks a mix that suits the coarse
  `type`, so somebody drafting a quiz from a novel never has to learn what
  `assertion_reason` means. Send them to be specific; leave them out to be quick.

  `type` on the RESPONSE is derived from the formats rather than echoed back from this
  request: an author who ticked only `long_answer` has written a subjective paper
  whatever the dropdown said, and the share link tells a prospective sitter which kind
  of paper they are opening before they commit to sitting it.

  `instructions` steers emphasis and wording. It is fenced off inside the prompt and
  cannot loosen the rule that every question comes from the chosen books — an
  instruction is a brief, not an escape hatch.
}
